WEBVTT

00:01.080 --> 00:03.250
There's one thing
I've come to understand.

00:03.920 --> 00:07.780
Hosen isn't taking
the points for himself.

00:07.790 --> 00:09.000
What do you mean?

00:09.000 --> 00:14.550
I thought the reason Hosen
only allowed partnerships to form...

00:14.550 --> 00:16.390
...if people paid
a high number of points

00:16.390 --> 00:18.890
was that he was
taking them for himself.

00:18.890 --> 00:22.730
But if that were the case,

00:22.730 --> 00:25.250
he should be more willing to pair up
with lower-ranked students.

00:25.260 --> 00:26.650
You're absolutely right.

00:27.300 --> 00:31.400
The penalty received
for failing is no joke.

00:31.400 --> 00:34.490
Just as Senior Ayanokoji deduced,

00:34.490 --> 00:38.160
Hosen isn't receiving anything
in return from our classmates.

00:38.160 --> 00:43.160
So he's simply ruling the class
and imposing rules on you, huh...

00:43.160 --> 00:49.090
And anyone who breaks
the rules gets shunned...

00:49.090 --> 00:54.590
But relationships built on points
can only be maintained by points.

00:55.130 --> 00:58.220
I want to build mutual trust
on equal footing.

00:59.890 --> 01:02.890
Let me speak with Hosen.

01:02.890 --> 01:05.349
I'm ready to talk right now.

01:05.349 --> 01:08.610
Understood.
I'll try calling him.

01:12.730 --> 01:15.360
Hosen is on the line.

01:15.360 --> 01:18.910
Yo, I heard a bit from Nanase.

01:18.910 --> 01:21.620
If possible, I'd like us
to meet and talk in person.

01:21.620 --> 01:23.870
Hah, no need for that.

01:23.870 --> 01:27.960
So you're not willing to negotiate?

01:27.960 --> 01:29.920
That's right.

01:29.920 --> 01:30.960
But, Hosen...

01:30.960 --> 01:34.460
Shut up. What right do you have
to talk to me like that?

01:34.460 --> 01:35.880
I'll kill you.

01:36.590 --> 01:38.510
I have no intention of being killed,

01:38.510 --> 01:40.970
but please meet with
Senior Horikita at least once.

01:40.970 --> 01:46.170
If you can't even prepare a decent amount
of points, don't contact me again.

01:48.770 --> 01:49.980
I'm so sorry!

01:50.900 --> 01:52.650
Please, raise your head.

01:52.650 --> 01:56.070
I'm grateful that you
went out of your way to help us.

01:56.070 --> 01:57.240
It really wasn't much...

01:57.240 --> 02:02.080
At the very least, we've conveyed
to Hosen what I want to do.

02:02.080 --> 02:03.990
That's enough for now.

02:12.170 --> 02:13.710
You're the outcast monster

02:13.710 --> 02:16.880
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

02:16.880 --> 02:18.760
Hidin', hidin'

02:20.340 --> 02:26.310
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

02:26.850 --> 02:30.190
Tell me what a genius is

02:30.190 --> 02:33.570
The one who creates singularities

02:33.570 --> 02:36.440
Don't you feed the monster

02:36.440 --> 02:42.490
The black outline has gotten bigger again

02:42.490 --> 02:46.580
Everyone is always the king's piece

02:46.580 --> 02:48.210
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

02:49.370 --> 02:53.130
How does it feel to see into the future?

02:53.130 --> 02:57.340
A monster made of lies

02:57.340 --> 03:01.390
The monster hidin, hidin',
go get him

03:01.390 --> 03:04.640
A twisted, unfair trigger

03:04.640 --> 03:08.060
Hidin', hidin', the maze thoughts

03:08.060 --> 03:11.140
Mysteries swimming in them

03:11.140 --> 03:14.190
Confused by truth and lies

03:14.190 --> 03:16.730
Are we the prey or the hunters?

03:17.480 --> 03:19.320
Hidin', hidin'

03:19.320 --> 03:20.740
Longing for the ordinary

03:20.740 --> 03:22.570
Hidin', hidin'

03:22.570 --> 03:24.370
Yes, you are the outcast monster

03:24.370 --> 03:30.960
Hidin', hidin', ding-ding-ding

03:37.500 --> 03:41.010
(#3 The Resolve of a Leader)

03:42.260 --> 03:43.760
(K. K)
(Incoming call)

03:43.760 --> 03:45.470
You took forever to pick up the phone!

03:45.470 --> 03:46.970
Sorry.

03:46.970 --> 03:50.270
So, did you find out about
what I asked this morning?

03:50.270 --> 03:53.770
I'm only calling because
I did a great job.

03:54.650 --> 03:59.530
According to the clerk, only one
has been sold since April this year.

04:00.280 --> 04:03.740
It seems a new student
tried to buy it,

04:03.740 --> 04:07.160
but after they finished paying,
another student approached them,

04:07.160 --> 04:09.790
and they ended up not buying it.

04:09.790 --> 04:12.870
What about the student
who asked for a refund?

04:12.870 --> 04:15.040
The clerk didn't know who it was.

04:15.040 --> 04:17.670
Apparently, it was a girl.

04:19.089 --> 04:21.630
Was my information helpful?

04:21.630 --> 04:24.800
Yeah, much more than I expected.

04:26.470 --> 04:29.220
I'm pretty capable, you know.

04:29.220 --> 04:31.180
You should be grateful.

04:31.180 --> 04:33.100
I am grateful.

04:33.100 --> 04:37.190
By the way, how are your
studies going, Kei?

04:37.190 --> 04:38.940
Well, um...

04:39.440 --> 04:44.070
It's just... if I go to the study group,
you won't be there, Kiyotaka.

04:44.570 --> 04:47.140
So you'll study hard if I'm there?

04:47.150 --> 04:48.200
Well yeah,

04:48.200 --> 04:51.830
I'd work hard in front of my boyfriend.

04:51.830 --> 04:55.580
In that case, want to come
to my room tomorrow?

04:55.580 --> 04:57.790
I can come hang out with you?!

04:57.790 --> 05:00.500
We're not going to hang out.
We're going to study.

05:03.670 --> 05:04.840
Koenji.

05:04.840 --> 05:08.550
It seems you still
haven't found a partner yet.

05:08.550 --> 05:10.600
And what of it?

05:10.600 --> 05:18.230
No matter who my partner is, scoring
above the passing mark is easy for me.

05:18.230 --> 05:22.480
In that case, would you let me
choose your partner for you?

05:22.480 --> 05:24.280
I must decline your offer.

05:24.280 --> 05:25.490
Why?

05:26.610 --> 05:29.120
Because I am who I am.

05:29.780 --> 05:31.490
Satisfied?

05:31.490 --> 05:32.700
Yes...

05:33.540 --> 05:35.160
For now.

05:42.380 --> 05:45.380
I-I'm sorry for keeping you waiting...

05:45.880 --> 05:47.380
Did something happen?

05:47.380 --> 05:51.890
I was trying to negotiate
and see if I could bring Hosen here.

05:51.890 --> 05:54.560
Seems like it didn't work.

05:54.560 --> 05:58.900
In that case, we'll have no choice but
to force a meeting with him ourselves.

05:58.900 --> 06:01.270
At this rate,
we'll remain in a stalemate.

06:01.270 --> 06:05.280
Then, will you please
listen to my proposal?

06:05.280 --> 06:10.990
I've concluded that Hosen's methods
won't carry us through what's ahead.

06:10.990 --> 06:12.660
It's a desperate measure,

06:12.660 --> 06:16.290
but I'd like to become
the leader of Class 1-D.

06:16.290 --> 06:17.910
Are you serious?

06:17.910 --> 06:23.920
That's a proposal that would
put far too much burden on you.

06:23.920 --> 06:25.550
It's fine.

06:25.550 --> 06:31.050
I don't want to lose the trust and
opportunity that Senior Horikita gave me.

06:31.050 --> 06:33.720
If you and Hosen come into conflict,

06:33.720 --> 06:37.640
the class won't come together,
and it will be split in two.

06:37.640 --> 06:39.690
I can't allow that.

06:39.690 --> 06:42.150
That's true, but...

06:42.150 --> 06:47.820
The problem of Class 1-D can be solved
if we get Hosen on our side.

06:47.820 --> 06:52.950
So, will you let me help
change his mind?

06:52.950 --> 06:54.490
It's a risky gamble.

06:54.910 --> 06:56.220
I'm prepared for that.

06:57.220 --> 06:58.470
Besides,

06:58.470 --> 07:03.000
I believe there's more than enough
possibility for us to work together.

07:03.000 --> 07:05.880
Even after he treated you like that?

07:05.880 --> 07:08.880
I'll take that as him
playing hard to get.

07:08.880 --> 07:10.550
For now, at least.

07:13.050 --> 07:18.270
Actually, I also thought persuading
Hosen would be the best option.

07:18.930 --> 07:23.360
If you leave it to me,
I'll make sure to bring Hosen to you...

07:23.360 --> 07:26.900
...the day after tomorrow,
on Sunday, Senior Horikita.

07:27.480 --> 07:29.400
I believe you.

07:29.950 --> 07:32.450
I'll look forward
to the day after tomorrow.

07:32.450 --> 07:34.410
Yes, I promise.

07:36.240 --> 07:37.540
What's up?

07:37.540 --> 07:39.750
It's time for the study group.

07:39.750 --> 07:43.630
Now that we've wrapped things up here,
can I leave the rest to you?

07:43.630 --> 07:44.630
Sure.

07:46.170 --> 07:49.170
Senior Horikita sure is busy.

07:49.170 --> 07:53.930
That's part of what
it means to lead a class.

07:54.510 --> 07:57.260
Senior Horikita is the class leader.

07:57.930 --> 07:59.180
But...

07:59.180 --> 08:01.810
What kind of person are you...

08:01.810 --> 08:03.650
...Senior Ayanokoji?

08:04.560 --> 08:07.600
I believe...

08:07.600 --> 08:13.060
you're an evil, disgusting human being.

08:14.220 --> 08:15.620
What do you mean?

08:16.740 --> 08:18.580
That's because...

08:18.580 --> 08:25.580
If she were from the White Room,
she would be observing me closely.

08:26.170 --> 08:31.090
To prove she's superior and...

08:31.090 --> 08:35.340
...to convince that man. But...

08:35.970 --> 08:39.100
For something said to someone
from the same White Room,

08:39.630 --> 08:41.600
it feels a bit off.

08:42.809 --> 08:45.600
I'm sorry.
Please forget what I said.

08:45.600 --> 08:48.820
Well then, Senior,
if you'll excuse me.

08:49.430 --> 08:50.360
Nanase.

08:51.230 --> 08:54.590
Do you know about
Protection Points?

08:54.590 --> 08:56.360
No, that's the first I've heard of them.

08:56.870 --> 09:01.490
It's a system that can nullify
expulsion if you use it.

09:03.240 --> 09:06.000
Why are you telling me this?

09:06.000 --> 09:08.750
Think of it as a return
for your cooperation.

09:08.750 --> 09:10.340
Thank you very much.

09:20.260 --> 09:25.390
There are lots of people coming and going
at this time, so I had to be careful.

09:25.390 --> 09:27.730
All right, let's get started.

09:27.730 --> 09:31.110
Huh? Aren't we going to
do something else first?

09:31.110 --> 09:33.280
If there are no problems
with your academics,

09:33.280 --> 09:36.280
we can chat as much as you want.

09:39.370 --> 09:40.530
Hey...

09:40.530 --> 09:43.700
Kiyotaka, your academic
ability is C, right?

09:43.700 --> 09:46.710
But you can actually do much
better than that, can't you?

09:46.710 --> 09:48.580
Something like that.

09:48.580 --> 09:51.040
Why are you hiding it so much?

09:51.040 --> 09:53.550
Because I didn't want to stand out.

09:54.800 --> 09:58.680
Then, if you got serious,
how many points could you get?

09:58.680 --> 10:00.180
400 points.

10:00.180 --> 10:02.930
Seriously?! 400 points...

10:02.930 --> 10:05.020
Since enrolling here,

10:05.020 --> 10:07.690
there hasn't been a single problem
I thought I couldn't solve.

10:09.690 --> 10:11.440
If you understand, let's begin.

10:15.030 --> 10:16.400
Over here.

10:17.650 --> 10:19.470
Teach me from beside me.

10:39.720 --> 10:40.470
Huh?

10:41.760 --> 10:43.640
What is this?

10:43.640 --> 10:45.350
Looks like a hair.

10:45.970 --> 10:48.350
A red hair!
And it's long!

10:48.350 --> 10:50.980
No matter how you look at it,
it has to be a girl's hair!

10:58.150 --> 11:01.410
Red hair!
A girl I haven't seen before!

11:03.220 --> 11:04.190
Who is it?!

11:04.190 --> 11:07.790
Huh?
This is Senior Ayanokoji's room, right?

11:10.120 --> 11:11.540
Sorry, it's me.

11:11.540 --> 11:12.880
What do you need?

11:12.880 --> 11:15.380
Oh, is someone there with you?

11:15.380 --> 11:17.380
Should I come back later?

11:19.130 --> 11:21.800
No, it's fine.
Come in.

11:24.640 --> 11:26.560
Pardon the intrusion!

11:26.560 --> 11:29.390
Hello, I'm Ichika Amasawa.

11:29.390 --> 11:30.980
Hi.

11:30.980 --> 11:34.610
You're my senior, right?
I'd love to know your name.

11:34.610 --> 11:36.480
Kei Karuizawa.

11:36.480 --> 11:38.280
Senior Karuizawa, huh?

11:38.280 --> 11:41.650
Oh! Could you be
Senior Ayanokoji's girlfriend?

11:41.650 --> 11:44.160
That's none of your business!

11:44.160 --> 11:47.660
More importantly, what's your
relationship with Kiyotaka?!

11:48.290 --> 11:50.960
I'll answer your question in a second,
so hold on, okay?

11:50.960 --> 11:54.330
I might have left something
behind in this room.

11:54.330 --> 11:56.540
It's my favorite hair tie.

11:56.540 --> 11:57.920
What?!

11:57.920 --> 12:00.920
I'm sure I took it off
when I was last here.

12:00.920 --> 12:04.300
It might be lying around somewhere.

12:05.430 --> 12:08.930
Senior, I feel like this might
look a little naughty.

12:10.430 --> 12:11.940
I'll try looking for it.

12:12.600 --> 12:15.690
Hey, answer my question.

12:16.690 --> 12:20.400
Hmm... how should I put it?

12:20.400 --> 12:24.200
Senior Ayanokoji is my... personal cook?

12:24.200 --> 12:26.370
Huh?!
What kind of answer is that?!

12:26.370 --> 12:28.200
She's Sudo's partner.

12:28.200 --> 12:30.580
I cooked for her once.

12:30.580 --> 12:33.870
Why did you cook for Sudo's partner?

12:35.830 --> 12:40.460
I'll check the kitchen, but please
keep searching over there, Senior.

12:40.460 --> 12:41.510
Got it.

12:42.130 --> 12:43.550
Hey!

12:43.550 --> 12:48.100
Like I told you, I invited her over and
cooked a meal for her once. That's all.

12:48.100 --> 12:52.020
Really? I should confirm
that with her myself.

12:52.020 --> 12:53.100
Ah, found it!

12:53.640 --> 12:56.600
Looks like it fell into
the gap next to the fridge.

12:56.600 --> 13:00.110
Seems like I interrupted something,
so I'll be on my way.

13:00.110 --> 13:02.360
Sorry things are so hectic.

13:02.360 --> 13:05.240
No, it's fine.
Well then, excuse me.

13:05.240 --> 13:08.780
But you really are smooth, Senior.

13:08.780 --> 13:12.000
I didn't expect you to have
a girlfriend that cute.

13:13.330 --> 13:19.000
Next time I have you cook for me, it might
be better if we're not alone together.

13:19.000 --> 13:20.500
Obviously!

13:20.500 --> 13:25.240
Then next time, Senior Karuizawa
can join us too!

13:25.240 --> 13:27.030
Goodbye!

13:28.140 --> 13:32.720
Looks like you've gotten acquainted
with a cute junior, huh, Kiyotaka.

13:39.520 --> 13:43.530
So far, 105 partnerships
have been formed.

13:43.530 --> 13:45.030
That's nearly 70%.

13:45.650 --> 13:48.870
If there's a White Room student
among the remaining ones,

13:48.870 --> 13:50.700
the probability is quite high.

13:51.410 --> 13:52.370
Oh my.

13:53.660 --> 13:56.250
If it isn't Ayanokoji.

13:56.250 --> 13:58.120
Sakayanagi.

13:58.120 --> 14:03.500
It seems you've been quite proactive
in engaging with the new students.

14:03.500 --> 14:08.890
I'm just helping Horikita find
partners for Sudo and Ike.

14:08.890 --> 14:10.090
I see.

14:10.600 --> 14:14.220
But is that really all there is to it?

14:14.220 --> 14:15.350
What do you mean?

14:15.350 --> 14:18.940
I was wondering
if perhaps the White Room...

14:18.940 --> 14:23.360
...had sent an assassin
to get you expelled.

14:23.360 --> 14:26.110
You don't have to worry about that.

14:26.110 --> 14:28.360
May I ask your reasoning?

14:28.360 --> 14:32.700
I'm going to abandon
my old way of thinking.

14:32.700 --> 14:36.370
I don't plan on holding back anymore.

14:37.500 --> 14:38.790
I see.

14:39.870 --> 14:43.500
If you haven't chosen a partner yet,

14:43.500 --> 14:45.880
may I offer my assistance?

14:45.880 --> 14:48.970
That's very generous of you.

14:48.970 --> 14:50.890
But I'll have to decline.

14:50.890 --> 14:54.640
Do you not trust my judgment?

14:54.640 --> 14:57.480
I acknowledge your abilities.

14:57.480 --> 15:01.150
But I'll decide my own fate.

15:01.150 --> 15:03.440
Is that so?

15:03.440 --> 15:06.280
Very well. I shall refrain from saying
anything improper.

15:06.280 --> 15:12.570
I'll watch from afar to see how
you fare in this battle, Ayanokoji.

15:16.660 --> 15:19.660
Excuse me, do you have a moment?

15:20.330 --> 15:24.670
You're Senior Ayanokoji
from Class 2-D, right?

15:25.710 --> 15:28.420
I'm Utomiya from Class 1-C.

15:28.420 --> 15:30.970
And this is Tsubaki.

15:30.970 --> 15:34.680
May we speak with you
about a partnership?

15:36.260 --> 15:39.930
Sorry, but we'd like to
get straight to the point.

15:41.190 --> 15:45.440
I don't like owing favors or being owed.

15:45.440 --> 15:48.940
I want a relationship that
won't come back to bite me.

15:49.490 --> 15:51.700
Can I ask something
that's been bothering me?

15:52.200 --> 15:53.700
Of course.

15:53.700 --> 15:57.330
Before coming to me, how many
people did you approach?

15:57.330 --> 16:02.580
I'm sorry.
Actually, you're the first.

16:02.580 --> 16:05.840
So I just happened
to be your first choice?

16:05.840 --> 16:08.750
It was a coincidence,
but there's also a reason.

16:08.750 --> 16:11.300
If we approached upperclassmen
from Class A or Class C,

16:11.300 --> 16:14.470
they might demand Private Points.

16:14.470 --> 16:17.220
I see, that makes sense.

16:17.810 --> 16:20.730
I don't currently have a partner,

16:20.730 --> 16:23.480
but I do have a potential candidate.

16:23.480 --> 16:27.480
We've agreed to see
if we can work well together.

16:27.480 --> 16:29.940
I see...

16:31.320 --> 16:33.360
Then it can't be helped.

16:34.610 --> 16:38.080
It'll probably be faster
to look for someone else.

16:38.080 --> 16:39.120
Yeah.

16:39.120 --> 16:42.870
Just in case,
here's my contact information.

16:42.870 --> 16:47.960
This may sound selfish,
but if I get turned down,

16:47.960 --> 16:50.380
I might reach out to you again.

16:50.380 --> 16:51.510
Understood.

16:52.260 --> 16:53.630
Let's go, Tsubaki.

16:55.010 --> 16:58.510
Sakurako Tsubaki and Riku Utomiya...

16:59.060 --> 17:01.310
I should remember those names.

17:03.520 --> 17:06.940
Sorry for calling you
out of the blue, Karuizawa.

17:06.940 --> 17:09.020
No, it's totally fine.

17:09.520 --> 17:11.819
So, what did you want to talk about?

17:12.530 --> 17:17.109
Karuizawa...
why did you break up with Hirata?

17:17.109 --> 17:19.660
Huh?
Didn't I already tell you?

17:19.660 --> 17:21.790
You did, but...

17:21.790 --> 17:24.619
Something about it
doesn't feel right.

17:24.619 --> 17:29.670
Did you break up because
you had a different goal in mind?

17:29.670 --> 17:34.170
What? I don't really get
what you're saying...

17:34.170 --> 17:38.800
Karuizawa...
are you dating Ayanokoji?

17:38.800 --> 17:40.100
Huh?

17:40.100 --> 17:42.060
So I was right after all!

17:42.060 --> 17:45.310
W-Wait, what?
Why would you think that?!

17:45.310 --> 17:51.320
When I asked you to help me get closer to
Ayanokoji, did you already like him?

17:51.320 --> 17:54.070
Or did you start
liking him before that?

17:54.070 --> 17:56.030
W-Wait! I...

17:56.030 --> 17:59.700
Tell me honestly! Otherwise...

17:59.700 --> 18:03.450
I won't be able to see you
as a friend anymore.

18:03.450 --> 18:05.870
That's...

18:08.250 --> 18:10.710
You're right, Sato.

18:10.710 --> 18:14.710
Ayano... I mean, I'm dating Kiyotaka.

18:15.670 --> 18:18.720
You even call him Kiyotaka, huh...

18:18.720 --> 18:23.850
We started dating
at the end of spring break.

18:23.850 --> 18:28.230
What I really want to know is
when you started liking him!

18:28.890 --> 18:31.230
I don't know. But...

18:31.230 --> 18:36.990
Around the time you came to me
for advice, I started to notice him.

18:36.990 --> 18:38.740
I see.

18:38.740 --> 18:41.160
You're mad at me, aren't you?

18:42.740 --> 18:44.780
I don't feel great about it.

18:44.780 --> 18:47.000
You knew how I felt,
but you went behind my back...

18:47.000 --> 18:50.790
But I got rejected by Ayanokoji.

18:50.790 --> 18:54.000
So I'm not really in a position
to be mad at you.

18:54.000 --> 18:55.130
But!

19:07.350 --> 19:11.810
Can you accept this as us
being even, Karuizawa?

19:13.110 --> 19:15.650
Want to hit me again?

19:15.650 --> 19:19.990
No, I don't think I have
the courage for that...

19:19.990 --> 19:23.160
I mean, I'm sorry for hitting you.

19:23.160 --> 19:26.580
No, I'm the one who should apologize.

19:26.580 --> 19:30.160
I'm sorry for falling for
the same person as you.

19:31.150 --> 19:32.800
I don't blame you for that.

19:32.810 --> 19:35.040
Ayanokoji is cool,

19:35.040 --> 19:38.170
and way more attractive than Hirata.

19:40.210 --> 19:41.180
Wha...

19:41.180 --> 19:43.430
What are you doing, Karuizawa?

19:44.800 --> 19:46.640
I'm really sorry...

19:54.190 --> 19:55.860
Sunday night.

19:56.400 --> 20:00.110
The day Nanase chose for
negotiations with Hosen has arrived.

20:02.360 --> 20:03.780
'Sup.

20:04.820 --> 20:07.370
Is your studying
for the test going well?

20:07.370 --> 20:09.250
Of course!

20:09.250 --> 20:14.130
Not to brag, but I'm planning to score
at least 250 points this time!

20:14.830 --> 20:17.420
Sounds like you've started
to enjoy studying.

20:17.420 --> 20:19.630
It's not that I like it.

20:20.300 --> 20:25.720
But just having Suzune praise me
gives me motivation.

20:27.100 --> 20:28.640
Hey, Ayanokoji...

20:29.220 --> 20:32.140
If I confessed to Suzune right now,

20:32.530 --> 20:35.650
do you think she'd say yes?

20:36.480 --> 20:37.980
Probably not.

20:39.150 --> 20:40.530
Figures.

20:42.150 --> 20:46.070
I've caused Suzune... No,

20:46.070 --> 20:48.950
I've caused the whole class
a lot of trouble until now.

20:48.950 --> 20:54.170
Even if I'm trying hard now, I don't think
that makes up for everything.

20:54.750 --> 20:59.420
But over the next two years,
I'll improve my strengths,

20:59.420 --> 21:01.920
and gradually fix my weaknesses.

21:01.920 --> 21:07.010
Then by the time we graduate,
I'm sure I'll be useful to the class.

21:07.890 --> 21:11.720
If you work hard and become
someone who contributes to the class,

21:11.720 --> 21:14.930
and Horikita still doesn't notice you,

21:14.940 --> 21:17.770
will you start hating studying?

21:17.770 --> 21:21.320
I might feel like I wanna die
and punch someone.

21:21.320 --> 21:25.950
But if I did that, Suzune would be
disappointed, right?

21:27.950 --> 21:30.120
Yeah, I don't want to do any of that.

21:34.210 --> 21:35.460
Sorry to keep you waiting.

21:35.460 --> 21:37.460
Shall we go?

21:41.880 --> 21:47.340
Do you really think we can make that
cocky first-year, Hosen, our ally?

21:47.340 --> 21:51.140
If I didn't think so,
we wouldn't be here.

21:51.140 --> 21:54.890
Sudo, don't say
anything unnecessary, okay?

21:54.890 --> 21:56.980
I-I got it, okay?

21:56.980 --> 21:59.360
Sorry to keep you waiting, Senior.

21:59.360 --> 22:01.320
Move, Nanase.

22:27.050 --> 22:33.680
Ah, eyes filled with a cold, dark light

22:33.680 --> 22:38.270
Lips that have swallowed all flavors,
yet remain empty

22:38.270 --> 22:42.600
"What could you be thinking?"

22:42.600 --> 22:47.040
It's so dim I can't see it

22:47.040 --> 22:52.830
The veil of a liar cannot be torn away

22:52.830 --> 22:58.460
Janus gazes at the room
where butterflies dance

22:58.460 --> 23:02.970
It's survival of the fittest out here

23:02.970 --> 23:08.010
One might already be gone by tomorrow

23:08.010 --> 23:13.180
I want to be buried,
I'm sure that's what I want

23:13.180 --> 23:18.320
With a knife of either
adoration or hatred, ah

23:18.320 --> 23:23.280
Not denying everything in this world

23:23.280 --> 23:30.070
Poison is medicine,
for the monster that devours everything

23:33.780 --> 23:36.830
I want to know what you really are
